  (:adr/body "
# ADR-2607175100: smtp.kotobase.net — kotobase-native mail

**Status**: accepted (design + Phase-1 integration landed)
**Date**: 2026-07-17
**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki
**Scope**: `gftdcojp/net-kotobase` product surface; DNS on `kotobase.net` zone;
substrate reuse of `kotoba-lang/mail` + `kotoba-lang/mailer` contracts.

## Context

Portfolio already has:

| Surface | Role |
|---|---|
| `mailer.gftd.ai` + Resend + CF Email Routing | **Org-internal** agent/app email (`*@mailer.gftd.ai`) |
| `kotoba-lang/mail` / `mailer` | Portable model + provider-request projection (no sockets) |
| `org-ietf-smtp` | RFC 5321 **client** (submission to a remote MTA) |
| workspace-compat (drive/docs/sheets/calendar) | Dual Google/MS skins; mailer is overlay not a new store |
| `kotobase.net` | Graph BaaS — storage/auth/quota, **not** previously an MTA |

Missing: a **product multi-tenant** mail edge on the kotobase domain so tenants
and actors can send/receive under kotobase DNS identity, with durable
inbound/outbound facts in their own kotoba graphs — without making
`mailer.gftd.ai` the only path, and without pretending CF Workers can listen
on TCP 25/465/587.

## Decision

### D1 — Hostnames

| Hostname | Role |
|---|---|
| **`smtp.kotobase.net`** | **Service host**: HTTPS XRPC submission API (Phase 1 primary). Phase 2 may also advertise RFC 5321 submission (port 587) on a non-Worker backend that fronts the same pipeline. |
| **`mail.kotobase.net`** | **Envelope domain**: default `From` / inbound addresses (`local@mail.kotobase.net`). MX → Cloudflare Email Routing → mail edge Worker. SPF/DKIM/DMARC live here. |
| `kotobase.net` apex | Unchanged graph BaaS; does **not** terminate SMTP. |

`smtp.kotobase.net` is **not** a claim that Workers speak SMTP wire protocol on
port 25. It is the **submission service name** (industry-common: `smtp.*` for
API/relay brands). Phase 1 transport is HTTPS. Phase 2 can add a real MTA
behind the same hostname without changing the XRPC contract.

### D2 — Relationship to `mailer.gftd.ai`

| | `mailer.gftd.ai` | `smtp.kotobase.net` |
|---|---|---|
| Audience | gftdcojp / etzhayyim **org agents** | **kotobase tenants** (product) |
| Default policy | Primary for `*@mailer.gftd.ai` org mail | Primary for `*@mail.kotobase.net` tenant mail |
| Store | PDS / emailBinding / existing relay | tenant graph `mail-v1` on kotobase |
| Auth | magatama / admin tokens | kotobase viewer + tenant CACAO |

No forced cutover. Org runbooks keep `mailer.gftd.ai`. Product docs and
workspace-compat mailer overlay point at kotobase mail NSIDs.

### D3 — Data plane (dedicated tenant graph)

Same scaling lesson as ADR-2606010500 / web+geo:

- Graph: `kotobase/db/<tenant-did>/mail-v1` (well-known `db_name` = `\"mail-v1\"`)
- Attributes (edge schema install vector):
  - `:mail.msg/id` (unique identity)
  - `:mail.msg/direction` (`\"inbound\"` | `\"outbound\"`)
  - `:mail.msg/message-id` (RFC Message-ID when known)
  - `:mail.msg/from` / `:mail.msg/to` / `:mail.msg/cc` / `:mail.msg/subject`
  - `:mail.msg/text` / `:mail.msg/html` (size-capped)
  - `:mail.msg/status` (`draft` | `queued` | `sent` | `failed` | `received` | `held`)
  - `:mail.msg/provider` / `:mail.msg/provider-id`
  - `:mail.msg/spf` / `:mail.msg/dkim` / `:mail.msg/dmarc` (inbound auth)
  - `:mail.msg/received-at` / `:mail.msg/sent-at`
  - `:mail.msg/owner` (tenant DID)
  - `:mail.bind/email` (unique) + `:mail.bind/did` + `:mail.bind/direction` + `:mail.bind/verified`
- Wire model for effects stays aligned with `mail.message` / `mail.inbound` /
  `mail.receipt` (ADR-2606301200). Edge may re-encode rather than depend on
  the JVM classpath of those libs inside the Worker.

### D4 — XRPC surface (`ai.gftd.apps.kotobase.mail.*`)

| NSID suffix | Kind | Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| `mail.send` | procedure (write) | Validate → optional approval gate → `mailer` provider request → host execute (Resend) → persist outbound + receipt |
| `mail.bind` | procedure (write) | Bind `local@mail.kotobase.net` (or verified custom domain later) to caller DID |
| `mail.ingestInbound` | procedure (write, edge/service-auth) | CF Email Worker → normalize → SPF/DKIM flags → tenant graph append |
| `mail.list` | procedure (read) | Datalog list over `mail-v1` (direction/status filters) |

Auth for `mail.send` / `mail.bind` / `mail.list`: same viewer resolution as
`web.ingest` / `geo.ingest` (JWT or CACAO). `mail.ingestInbound` uses a
service credential (Worker-to-Worker / admin) — not end-user bearer.

### D5 — Provider boundary (Phase 1 / 2)

```text
Phase 1 (now):
  mail.send
    → validate + bind check
    → mailer request shape (:resend HTTP POST https://api.resend.com/emails)
    → edge net/fetch with secrets/get:resend-api-key (RESEND_API_KEY)
    → receipt → datomic.transact on mail-v1

  inbound:
    MX mail.kotobase.net → CF Email Routing
      → account email() Worker (net-kotobase-mail or email-relay sibling)
      → mail.ingestInbound → mail-v1

Phase 2 (optional):
  Real RFC 5321 submission listener (non-Worker host) on smtp.kotobase.net:587
    AUTH maps API key / CACAO → same mail.send pipeline
  Optional SES / self-hosted MTA as alternate mailer provider
```

Cloudflare Workers **cannot** accept SMTP on 25/465/587. Phase 2 is an
explicit non-Worker deploy; Phase 1 does not block product use.

### D6 — Address policy

- Default mailbox domain: `mail.kotobase.net`.
- `from` on `mail.send` must be a **bound** address for the caller DID
  (`mail.bind` with `verified=true`), or an allowlisted platform address for
  operators.
- Local-part rules: `[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,63}` (no leading `.`, no `..`).
- Custom domains (tenant brings MX/SPF to their zone) are a follow-up; schema
  leaves room via bind records with non-`mail.kotobase.net` emails.

### D7 — GEWP

GEWP (ADR-2605141800) remains the **agent wire format** for structured
agent↔agent mail. `smtp.kotobase.net` accepts plain human mail and may
**pass through** a GEWP MIME part when present (`application/vnd.gewp+json`)
as attachment/metadata on the stored entity — Core Conformant parsing is
not required for Phase 1 human mail.

### D8 — DNS (kotobase.net zone)

```text
; submission API (Phase 1 HTTPS)
smtp.kotobase.net.     CNAME/Custom Domain → net-kotobase Worker
                       (or dedicated net-kotobase-smtp route)

; envelope domain
mail.kotobase.net.     MX 10  <cloudflare-email-routing>
mail.kotobase.net.     TXT    \"v=spf1 include:resend.com -all\"
resend._domainkey.mail.kotobase.net.  CNAME  <resend DKIM>
_dmarc.mail.kotobase.net. TXT \"v=DMARC1; p=quarantine; rua=mailto:dmarc@mail.kotobase.net\"
```

Exact Resend DNS targets come from the Resend dashboard at provision time;
ADR freezes **names and roles**, not Resend's rotating CNAME values.

### D9 — Non-goals (this ADR)

- Full Google Workspace / M365 UI replacement.
- IMAP/JMAP server on kotobase (clients use API / future gateway).
- Replacing `mailer.gftd.ai` for org-internal agents.
- Running a public open relay (AUTH + bind + quota required).
- Force-push / rewriting historical M365 archives.

## Consequences

- kotobase tenants get a first-class mail product edge on the same domain
  family as graph storage.
- Outbound durability is content-addressed in the tenant graph (audit/query).
- `mailer.gftd.ai` stays the org default; product and org paths diverge cleanly.
- Phase 1 ships without waiting for a TCP MTA; Phase 2 can add real SMTP
  submission without renaming the service.

## Implementation map

| Artifact | Location |
|---|---|
| This ADR (superproject) | `90-docs/adr/2607175100-smtp-kotobase-net.edn` |
| Repo-local ADR | `orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/docs/adr/2607175100-smtp-kotobase-net.md` |
| Pure domain | `clj-edge/src/kotobase/mail.cljc` |
| Handlers | `clj-edge/src/kotobase/domain_search.cljc` (+ worker NSID wiring) |
| Lexicons | `contracts/lexicons/ai/gftd/apps/kotobase/mail/*.json` |
| Schema | `kotobase.schema/mail-v1-schema` |
| Substrate (unchanged) | `kotoba-lang/mail`, `kotoba-lang/mailer` |

## Status of landings

- Design: accepted (this ADR).
- Phase-1 code: pure core + lexicons + worker NSID hooks + tests in
  `net-kotobase` branch `agent/smtp-kotobase`.
- Live DNS / Resend domain verify / CF Email Routing catch-all: **operator
  provision step** (not auto-applied by code merge).
")
